Could you include it in the patch as a document put in Documentation
directory?  Also don't forget to update ALSA-Configuration.txt when an
option is added/modified.


> Takashi,
> I've not added a "true" quirk (function pointer parameter) to the
> "parse_audio_endpoints" function. Instead I've just made the quirk fit into
> a simple function so that parse_audio_enpoints needs only 2 lines of patch.
>  - Do you still think it's necessary to implement a "true" quirk?

The patch itself is small and clean enough to include.

But I still think it'd be better to split it off to another module so
that more intuitive options could be used rather than a magical
number.

About the patch:  Could you fix the following?


> --- usbaudio.c	2006-03-05 21:41:48.000000000 +0100
> +++ /usr/src/alsa/alsa-cvs-02282006.patched/alsa-driver/usb/usbaudio.c	2006-03-05 21:52:14.000000000 +0100
> @@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
>  #else
>  0; /* disabled as default for buggy async-unlink handling */
>  #endif
> +static int device_setup = 0x00; /* device specific setup (parameter's meaning depends on the physical devicer) */

You don't need zero-initialization here.  A static variable is
guaranteed to be zero-initialized.

Also, try not to exeed 80 columns in general :)

>  /*
> @@ -2547,6 +2550,7 @@
>  	return 0;
>  }
>  
> +int audiophile_skip_setting_quirk(int iface, int altno);

Please make it a static function.

> @@ -2585,6 +2589,10 @@
>  		stream = (get_endpoint(alts, 0)->bEndpointAddress & USB_DIR_IN) ?
>  			SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE : SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK;
>  		altno = altsd->bAlternateSetting;
> +	
> +		/* quirk for audiophile usb: skip AltSets not corresponding to device_setup */
> +		if (chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0763, 0x2003) && 
> +		    audiophile_skip_setting_quirk(iface_no,altno)) continue;

Put continue to the next line.

@@ -3112,6 +3120,35 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
> +int audiophile_skip_setting_quirk(int iface, int altno) {
> +	if (device_setup & AUDIOPHILE_SET) {
> +		if ((device_setup & AUDIOPHILE_SET_DTS) && altno != 6) return 1;	
Put return to the next line (in other places, too).


Thanks,

Takashi


